# CHECKPOINTS — Final State Evaluation

> The path is not evaluated, the destination is. These are objective
> checkpoints a human or an agent can use to decide if the project is healthy.

## C1 — Harness is complete

- [ ] `AGENTS.md`, `scripts/harness.mjs`, `scripts/harness-lib.mjs`,
      `scripts/build_harness.mjs`, `activities.json`, `progress/current.md` exist.
- [ ] `{{DOCS_DIR}}/harness/architecture.md`, `conventions.md`, `structure.md`,
      `development.md`, `testing.md`, `verification.md` exist.
- [ ] `{{HARNESS_CMD}}` exits with code 0.
- [ ] `node --test scripts/harness-lib.spec.mjs` exits with code 0.

## C2 — State is coherent

- [ ] At most one activity is `in_progress` in `activities.json`.
- [ ] Every `done` task ran its level (`--for-task`); every `done` full-level
      activity ran the full harness once at close.
- [ ] Every `done` activity has associated passing tests.
- [ ] `progress/current.md` is empty or describes the active session.

## C3 — Code respects architecture

- [ ] `{{SOURCE_DIR}}` only contains modules described in
      `{{DOCS_DIR}}/harness/architecture.md` and `structure.md`.
- [ ] No new dependency outside the manifest without review.
- [ ] No stray debug output, no TODOs without context.

## C4 — Verification is real

- [ ] The source tree has tests covering the public behavior.
- [ ] Type checks pass for every configured package.
- [ ] Tests mock external boundaries only; no real network calls.
- [ ] `{{TEST_CMD}}` shows > 0 tests and all green.
- [ ] The production build succeeds.

## C5 — Session closed properly

- [ ] No suspicious untracked files (`*.tmp`, build artifacts outside ignores).
- [ ] `progress/history.md` has an entry for the last session.
- [ ] The last worked activity reflects its correct state.
- [ ] No secrets, credentials or generated output are tracked.

---

**How to use this file:** the reviewer goes through each checkbox, marks `[x]`
or `[ ]`, and rejects session close if any C1–C5 box remains empty.
